8
00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:34.570
So let's talk about flow.

9
00:00:34.570 --> 00:00:40.509
As we saw when we were debugging, flow always reads from left to right, so just make sure

10
00:00:40.509 --> 00:00:45.310
your Blueprints are always set up in such a way where the information is readable, we've

11
00:00:45.310 --> 00:00:50.880
not got crossing wires, and that all your information is going from left to right.

12
00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.740
Events are functions that are often triggered by external influences, so as we saw before

13
00:00:55.740 --> 00:01:00.920
when we added beginOverlap and endOverlap, they were impacted by the player overlapping

14
00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:03.579
them, which is what we mean by external influences.

15
00:01:03.579 --> 00:01:07.299
Something has happened that has caused this event to fire.

16
00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:12.799
We can do functions of macros, similar to C++, which was a little bit outside the scope

17
00:01:12.799 --> 00:01:17.700
of this tutorial, but again we can still do functions of macros within Blueprints.

18
00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.159
And we have input and output on the right side of nodes.

19
00:01:21.159 --> 00:01:26.439
So you've got inputs on this side, which is the string, so we're printing in a string

