00:01:26.439 --> 00:01:31.000
that says out in this instance, bad choice of wording there, but I think you understand

21
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:32.000
what I mean.

22
00:01:32.019 --> 00:01:37.379
And then you've also got the outputs on the right hand side there.

23
00:01:37.379 --> 00:01:42.579
We've got a whole list of different Blueprint variables, again we used a boolean in our example,

24
00:01:42.579 --> 00:01:47.939
we also used a door reference, but you can get bytes, integers, names, vectors, enums,

25
00:01:47.939 --> 00:01:49.780
whole list of things here.

26
00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:55.319
And as you continue your Blueprint journey, you'll get more familiar with these concepts,

27
00:01:55.319 --> 00:02:01.420
and also we got a variable and we set a variable, so we call them getters and setters,

28
00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:04.959
